A||N||4||contra||How do i replace my heater coil?||||1||
Z||000000||contra||10-05-2000||06:19 PM||||*(oops my mistake, i meant heater core, not coil...oh well)*<P>i want to remove the heater core from my parts car and put it in my GT, because i think my core is leaking or is dying.<BR>Is there any instructions? thanks<P><p>[This message has been edited by contra (edited 10-05-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Patrick||10-05-2000||06:55 PM||||<BR>The <B>Search</B> function works like lightning now. Try looking for <I>heater</I>. Don't forget the archived threads.||||reg||1
Z||000002||My7Fieros||10-05-2000||07:12 PM||||Take out the windshield washer fluid container first, this allows you access to the two hoses that connect to the heater core. Once you put the washer fluid container to the side, you'll see the two hoses. Unclamp the hoses and pull them off.<BR>Next go inside the car on the pass side...under the dash you'll see a black box hanging...take off the two screws (that are visible) and the right side of that black box will swing open...you'll then see the heater core. <BR>Theres a metal "strap" of sorts holding the core in place...unscrew the two screws (upper and lower) on the clamp, and pull out the core and replace...its no big deal.<BR>The only part that may be difficult is pulling the hoses off up front...some times it is, some times it isnt.<BR>Reassemble....thats it!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||ROB MAC||10-05-2000||11:35 PM||||Might be a good idea to have a rad shop pressure test that core before you go to all the trouble to install. A stitch in time!||||reg||1
Z||000004||Tigger||10-06-2000||12:32 AM|||| <IMG SRC="http://watchsnmor.tripod.com/fiero090.jpg"> <P>You mean this thingy?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> j/k<P>Haynes manual I think has good instructions or search the threads.  You'll need to drain most of the radiator fluid first to get it below the core level.  It's jam packed under the dash so you'll probably want to drain probably close to all of it.  There are some screws that hold a panel on under the dash, the core is behind that.  You'll need to unhook the heater hoses from the front compartment and the heater core will come out from under the dash.  Install it reverse, don't forget you'll need to "burp" the coolant when you refill too.  Hope this helps...<P>------------------<BR>T-T-F-N, Tah Tah For Now!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tigger.gif">          <BR> <A HREF="mailto:RacingStripes@hotmail.com">RacingStripes@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||1
